            <div xml:id="d916">

                <pb facs="0788" n="776" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg776"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.51/2642a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Messersmith</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-09-04T14:00:00-04:00">September 4, 1940—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>144. Your 96, September 3, 4 p.m.<anchor n="67" xml:id="d916-f1"/> I shall look
                    forward to discussing with you in Washington when you arrive our relations with
                    Cuba. In the meantime no decision will be taken with respect to the Cuban
                    request for a loan.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
